A line is parameterized, with a direction vector of the form $\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ b \end{pmatrix}.$ Find the value of $b$.

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair A, B, L, R;
int i, n;

for (i = -8; i <= 8; ++i) {
  draw((i,-8)--(i,8),gray(0.7));
  draw((-8,i)--(8,i),gray(0.7));
}

draw((-8,0)--(8,0),Arrows(6));
draw((0,-8)--(0,8),Arrows(6));

A = (-3,-2);
B = (1,4);
L = extension(A, B, (0,8), (1,8));
R = extension(A, B, (0,-8), (1,-8));

draw(L--R, blue);

label("$x$", (8,0), E);
label("$y$", (0,8), N);
[/asy]

In a given cube, all eight vertices are tangent to a sphere with radius $r$. Three mutually perpendicular planes, each of which contains four of the vertices of the cube, are also tangent to three spheres, each with radius $R$. All four spheres are externally tangent to a fifth sphere with radius $s$. Find the relationship between the radii $r$, $R$, and $s$.

[asy]
size(200);
import three;

currentprojection = orthographic(0,1,0.3);

path3 to画(cubeFrame, int order, int N, bool drawlines, bool dotnodes)
{
triple[] P;
P.push((0,0,0)); P.push((1,0,0)); P.push((1,1,0)); P.push((0,1,0));
P.push((0,0,1)); P.push((1,0,1)); P.push((1,1,1)); P.push((0,1,1));

for(int i = 0; i < N; ++i)
{
if(i == order)
{
dot(P[i]);
label("$A_" + string(i) + "$", P[i], dir(P[i]));
}
if(drawlines)
{
for(int j = 0; j < N; ++j)
{
if(i!= j && abs(P[i] - P[j]) <= 1.1)
draw(P[i]--P[j]);
}
}
}
return P;
}

draw(cubeFrame,0,8,true,true);

triple O = (0.5,0.5,0.5);
dot(O); label("$O$",O,S);

triple p1 = (0.2,0.2,0.2);
dot(p1); label("$E$",p1,S);
draw(Circle(O,0.3)); draw(Circle(p1,0.3));

triple p2 = (0.2,0.8,0.2);
dot(p2); label("$F$",p2,S);
draw(Circle(p2,0.3));

triple p3 = (0.8,0.2,0.2);
dot(p3); label("$G$",p3,S);
draw(Circle(p3,0.3));

triple p4 = (0.2,0.2,0.8);
dot(p4); label("$H$",p4,S);
draw(Circle(p4,0.3));

triple centerOfSphere = (0.5,0.5,0.2);
dot(centerOfSphere); label("$I$",centerOfSphere,S);
draw(Circle(centerOfSphere,0.3));

[/asy]

In the figure, $PQ$ is tangent to semicircle $QBR$ at point $Q$ and $PR$ is tangent to semicircle $RAS$ at point $R$.  If arc $RB$ measures $65^\circ$ and arc $SA$ measures $72^\circ$, then find $\angle QPR$, in degrees.

[asy]
import graph;

unitsize(1.5 cm);

pair A, B, P, Q, R, S;
pair[] O;
real[] r;

r[1] = 1;
r[2] = 0.8;

B = (-2*r[2],0);
O[2] = (-r[2],0);
R = (0,0);
O[1] = (r[1],0);
S = (2*r[1],0);
A = O[1] + dir(180 + 72)*r[1];
Q = O[2] + dir(-65)*r[2];
P = extension(Q, Q + rotate(90)*(Q - O[2]), A, A + rotate(90)*(A - O[1]));

draw(B--S);
draw(arc(O[2],r[2],180,360));
draw(arc(O[1],r[1],180,360));
draw(A--P--Q);

label("$A$", A, NE);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$P$", P, N);
label("$Q$", Q, SE);
label("$R$", R, dir(270));
label("$S$", S, SE);
[/asy]

